1
00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:04,780
A few days ago, my neighbor, who lives alone, had to go to the hospital.

2
00:00:05,780 --> 00:00:08,440
He called for help himself. But I kept wondering:

3
00:00:10,340 --> 00:00:11,400
what if he couldn't?

4
00:00:11,960 --> 00:00:13,500
No one would have known.

5
00:00:16,040 --> 00:00:19,800
So my teammate and I built RUOK, short for "Are you okay?"

6
00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:28,200
We designed the device on a Raspberry Pi Zero 2,
and my teammate soldered every part by hand.

7
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,460
Inside are a 24-gigahertz radar sensor that detects movement,

8
00:00:36,580 --> 00:00:39,800
and a microphone that only measures how loud the room is.

9
00:00:45,420 --> 00:00:49,640
There's no camera, nothing to wear,
and no audio is ever recorded.

10
00:00:54,110 --> 00:00:55,490
This is the guardian app.

11
00:00:55,930 --> 00:00:58,250
Mom's Room is green, so everything is normal.

12
00:01:01,270 --> 00:01:06,790
The Living Room shows a warning:
no motion or voice for a while.

13
00:01:08,450 --> 00:01:10,300
And Dad's Room is offline.

14
00:01:12,140 --> 00:01:15,020
Adding a device takes seconds. Give it a name,

15
00:01:15,240 --> 00:01:18,400
and the server creates a unique ID and a secure token.

16
00:01:24,520 --> 00:01:27,180
In this demo, the sensor data is simulated.

17
00:01:30,120 --> 00:01:37,360
When something is wrong, RUOK creates an alert,
like "Device offline" or "No activity."

18
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:43,920
If the silence continues, the alert becomes urgent.

19
00:01:48,410 --> 00:01:49,300
RUOK:

20
00:01:49,830 --> 00:01:52,110
independence for seniors, peace of mind for families.

21
00:01:52,830 --> 00:01:54,000
Thank you.

